# UI screen specification rules

When designing, documenting, or implementing a **screen** (page or full-view route), capture the following. Use this as a checklist for PRs and for AI-assisted changes so behavior stays explicit.

## Screen

- **Name / route**: e.g. `/`, `/legal/privacy`
- **Purpose**: One sentence—what job this screen does for the user
- **Primary user**: Who uses it and in what situation

## Layout

Describe structure in **top → middle → bottom** (or scrolling regions if one column). Call out fixed vs scrollable areas, safe areas on mobile, and max widths on desktop.

- **Top section**: title, nav, filters, summary
- **Middle section**: main content, lists, forms, player
- **Bottom section**: primary actions, tab bar, persistent controls

## Buttons and clickable items

For **each** interactive control (button, link, list row, icon), specify:

| Field | Rule |
|--------|------|
| **Name** | Visible label or accessibility name |
| **Position** | Relative to layout section (e.g. bottom bar, header right) |
| **Action on tap** | What the app does (submit, toggle, play, open picker) |
| **Destination** | Route, modal, sheet, external URL, or “none” if in-place |
| **Navigation type** | `push`, `replace`, `back`, `modal`, `sheet`, `deeplink`, `none` |
| **Data passed** | IDs, query params, route state, or context—be explicit |
| **Visible when** | Feature flags, auth, content exists, edit mode, etc. |
| **Disabled when** | Loading, invalid form, offline, permissions |
| **Success behavior** | Navigate, toast, refresh list, close modal, play audio |
| **Error behavior** | Inline message, toast, retry affordance—no silent failure |

Prefer one row per control in design notes or PR description; reuse the same table in code comments only when it prevents regression.

## Back behavior

- **Hardware / gesture back**: Where it returns (parent route vs exit app) and whether state is preserved
- **In-app back affordance**: Matches platform expectation (stack pop vs up to parent)
- **Unsaved changes**: Confirm discard, save draft, or auto-save—state explicitly

## Implementation alignment

- Interactive elements must have **matching** `aria-label` or visible text to the **Name** above when the control is icon-only or ambiguous
- **Disabled when** must be reflected in real UI (disabled/aria-disabled), not only ignored clicks
- **Navigation type** and **Destination** should match Next.js `Link`, `router.push/replace`, or Capacitor/navigation patterns used elsewhere in the app
